.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_OPEN_PATCH 3 2026-11-03 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_open_patch \- compose opened MPQ archives into an owned reader.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_open_patch("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s **" "archive,"
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "base,"
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *const *" "patch_archives,"
.BI "        const char *const *" "patch_prefixes,"
.BI "        size_t " "patch_count"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compose the opened \fIbase\fP with \fIpatch_count\fP ordered layers from
\fIpatch_archives\fP. Later layers override earlier ones. COPY and BSD0
payloads are validated against their before/after MD5 values; ordinary added
members and delete markers are supported. Explicit addition-only layers need
no fabricated patch metadata marker.
.PP
Zero layers create an independent byte-preserving snapshot of the base's
logical backing source. The layer array may be NULL in this case. Changed
modern views use the existing private v3 materialization; this does not
change the generation of any physical input archive.
.PP
A NULL \fIpatch_prefixes\fP array or a NULL entry requests deterministic
prefix inference for that layer. An empty string selects the root namespace.
Explicit prefixes must agree with available namespace metadata; conflicting
or ambiguous metadata is rejected. Game-specific prefix inference, filename
recovery, and locale selection are not provided. Named v3/v4 materialization
requires complete, unambiguous names and representable metadata.
.PP
Input archives are borrowed synchronously, remain unchanged, and are never
closed by this function. Their callback contexts must remain valid during
composition and for their own normal archive lifetimes. After success, the
result retains neither input sources, callback contexts, nor MPQE credential
buffers. Inputs may be closed and their callback contexts released.
.PP
The result is an ordinary independently owned, read-only archive. Close it
with \fBlibmpq__archive_close\fP(). Independently owned clones and streams
remain usable after parent closure. Private temporary storage is retained
until the final dependent source closes. Cleanup is best effort on persistent
I/O failure; secure deletion and crash recovery are not guaranteed. Concurrent
close/read operations require external synchronization.
.PP
Verify physical signatures and RAW_MD5 on the original input handles.
Composition does not inherit their trust as verification of the logical
output. A changed v3 materialization does not retain physical v4 raw digests.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Success returns 0 and sets *\fIarchive\fP to a non-NULL owned reader.
Failure returns an existing negative error code and clears *\fIarchive\fP
when the output pointer is supplied. No partially usable result is returned.
.SH ERRORS
NULL required arguments, missing layer arrays, or invalid input handles
return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP. An oversized layer count returns
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE\fP. Invalid patches, digest mismatches, unsupported
identities, or namespace conflicts return the existing format or decoding
error. Source, temporary-storage, allocation, and cleanup errors propagate.
Input archives remain caller-owned on every error path.
